$DIR/main.p:7:2: cannot store unsafe.String(&buf[0], 4) in package variable name, which outlives buf
    unsafe.String(&buf[0], 4) points into buf. buf is a local array of main
    (declared at main.p:6). When main returns, buf's memory is reclaimed, but
    package variables live for the whole program, so package variable name would
    be left pointing at reclaimed memory.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Store values instead of views of buf, or allocate buf and store its owner,
    an owned[[4]byte], which moves there:
        name = new([4]byte)
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3002" for a longer explanation)
